  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.8.11 - on SpawnDev.ILGPU 5.4.24; faster CUDA decode and a CUDA correctness fix. qwen3:1.7b Q4_K_M on an RTX 4070 decodes at ~235 tok/s at a short prompt and ~219 at an 1,800-token prompt (5.8.10: ~213 / ~200). Fix: with FP contraction on (the default since 5.8.7), a model loaded with joined q|k|v projections drifted ~3e-4 from the same model with separate ones on CUDA (the rotation was fused differently in two kernels); both routes are bit-identical again. Faster: the top-64 candidate selection on group kernels (CUDA + WebGPU, ~170 -> 20 us a step), the Q6_K LM head issues fewer instructions (-15%, bit-identical), qwen3's q/k head norms in one launch, v's projection GEMV on a second stream beside q|k (CUDA graph fork / join, +4% decode), and on WebGPU the group attention merge. The speedups keep greedy output identical; the fix moves CUDA logits by up to ~3e-4 (toward the separate-projection result). Env switches (GGUF_TOPK_GROUP, GGUF_OVERLAP_V, GGUF_ATTN_COMBINE_GROUP) are the A/B. See CHANGELOG.md.",
